# Private dilemmas: only the owner of {A} sees the choice; the astronaut decides in
# character if nobody answers. Both options are decent; the cost is the point.
# House style: content/STYLE.md.

card dil_dose
type dilemma
days 6 30
weight 8
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
lean warm report keep
text {A}'s dosimeter reads higher than anyone else's, probably because the bunk sits close to the hull. Moving it means telling the flight surgeon, who will want a meeting.
option report | Tell the surgeon | The meeting has a 40-minute round trip on every question. {A}'s bunk moves two meters closer to the water tanks, and the reading drops by a third.
  morale A -2
  trait A warm 2
option keep | Keep it quiet | {A} logs it privately and moves the sleeping bag to the other wall. It isn't nothing. It isn't a meeting either.
  set dose_hidden
  who dose_who A

card dose_swap
type beat
due
once
days 14 40
roles A B
when flag dose_hidden
when is A dose_who
when same A B
when cond B ok
text {B} reads the dosimeter logs the way other people read the news, and notices {A}'s numbers. Without a word, {B} swaps bunks with {A} that night. By morning the readings are even.
do bond A B 10
do bond B A 6

card dil_gains
type dilemma
days 5 32
weight 9
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
lean brave tune wait
text The attitude control on {A}'s ship has a slow wobble, and {A} seems to be the only one who notices it. A small adjustment would probably settle it. Procedure says any change needs ground sign-off, and the ground is 20 minutes away and asleep.
option tune | Adjust it now | {A} makes the change, watches the wobble die away over six cycles, and writes it down before anyone can ask. The ground signs off in the morning with a single word: "Nice."
  set gains_tuned
  who gains_who A
  trait A brave 2
option wait | Wait for sign-off | {A} files the request and lives with the wobble overnight. The ground approves the exact change {A} proposed, word for word, 14 hours later.
  trait A brave -2
  morale A 2

card gains_payoff
type event
due
once
days 18 40
roles A
when flag gains_tuned
when is A gains_who
when cond A ok
text On the big correction burn, the attitude trace from {A}'s ship is a flat line. Every other ship shows the same slow wobble {A} found. By the next burn, {A}'s numbers are running on all seven.
do morale A 5
do res fuel 1

card dil_manual
type dilemma
days 3 34
weight 8
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
lean curious manual auto
text The cabin humidity control on {A}'s ship is hunting, swinging wet and then dry every few minutes. {A} could put it in manual and hold it by hand, just for a minute. Everyone knows how "just for a minute" goes.
option manual | Take it in manual | Just for a minute turns into most of a shift. {A} holds humidity within a percent by hand and finds the cause: a sensor sitting in the steam from the galley kettle. The sensor moves, and the control goes back to auto.
  trait A curious 3
  morale A -1
option auto | Leave it in auto | {A} leaves the controller alone and logs every swing. The pattern lines up with the galley schedule. The kettle moves, the controller settles, and it never knows how close it came.
  morale A 2

card dil_bracket
type dilemma
days 8 36
weight 8
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
lean brave zip ticket
text {A} finds a hairline crack in a bracket holding a stowage rack, at a corner the model said would carry no stress. A proper fix means opening a ticket with Earth. A zip-tie fix takes five minutes.
option ticket | Open a ticket | Earth wants photos, measurements, and a part number nobody can find. {A} supplies all three. The approved repair arrives a few days later and is, in every way that matters, a zip tie.
  morale A -1
option zip | Zip-tie it | {A} redesigns the mount on the spot with zip ties and spite. It is ugly, and it will outlast the ship.
  set zip_fix
  res spares -1
  morale A 3

card dil_letter
type dilemma
days 10 38
weight 7
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
lean warm now save
text A data packet from home arrives for {A}, flagged personal. Reading it now means reading it on a cramped ship with no privacy. Saving it means carrying it unread until a quiet moment that may never come.
option now | Read it now | {A} reads it in the airlock, the only place aboard with a door. {A} comes out ten minutes later, doesn't say what it said, and makes everyone coffee.
  morale A 6
option save | Save it | {A} saves it for a bad day. Every mission has one, and now {A} has something set aside for it.
  set letter_saved
  who letter_who A

card letter_open
type beat
due
once
days 20 41
roles A
when flag letter_saved
when is A letter_who
when morale A <= 52
text It's a bad day, the kind {A} saved the letter for. {A} reads it in the airlock and then goes back to work. Whatever it said, it was enough.
do morale A 12

card dil_eva_cam
type dilemma
days 7 33
weight 7
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
lean brave go wait
text An external camera on {A}'s ship has frosted over. Clearing it means an unscheduled EVA. Nobody would blame {A} for waiting for the planned one.
option go | Go out now | {A} clears the lens in twenty minutes and, before coming in, takes a photo of the fleet strung out against the dark. It becomes everyone's wallpaper.
  trait A brave 3
  morale A 4
option wait | Wait for the planned EVA | {A} waits. The camera stays blind for a few days, which is exactly what the risk assessment called acceptable. {A} has read the risk assessment twice.
  trait A brave -2

card dil_credit
type dilemma
days 9 36
weight 6
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
lean warm let correct
text Mission Control credits the fix for last week's scrubber fault to the wrong ship. {A} did the work. Correcting the record means a formal message, a 40-minute round trip, and a form.
option correct | Correct the record | {A} sends the form. Mission Control replies with a correction and an apology, both on the same form.
  morale A 2
option let | Let it go | {A} lets it go. The other ship's crew find out anyway and send the good coffee across on the next transfer.
  morale A 4
  trait A warm 2

card dil_interlock
type dilemma
days 4 36
weight 8
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
lean brave override vote
text The airlock on {A}'s ship won't cycle. One door sensor says "closed". The other says "ajar". The door is obviously closed, and {A} has the override code.
option override | Use the override | {A} overrides, cycles the lock, and opens a ticket straight away. The sensor was right: a seal had crept a millimeter. {A} reseats it before anyone needs that airlock in a hurry.
  trait A brave 2
option vote | Find a third opinion | {A} pulls the lock's pressure trace as a tiebreaker. The door is sealed, and the "ajar" sensor is lying. {A} swaps it, the interlock is satisfied, and nobody overrode anything.
  trait A curious 2
  res spares -1
